From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: nt36536: accept pen report format 0x02

The Lenovo Tab Pen Plus (AP500U) sends its reports with format id 0x02
in point_data[66]. The driver only parsed 0x01 and dropped every other
id with "Unknown pen format id!", so the pen did nothing. The 0x02
report has the same layout as 0x01, so parse both.

Link: https://github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux/issues/16
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
index 3c0650a7aa..d198b60b8f 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
@@ -1012,7 +1012,7 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 		// parse and handle pen report
 		pen_format_id = point_data[66];
 		if (pen_format_id != 0xFF) {
-			if (pen_format_id == 0x01) {
+			if (pen_format_id == 0x01 || pen_format_id == 0x02) {
 				// report pen data
 				pen_x = (uint32_t)(point_data[67] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[68]);
 				pen_y = (uint32_t)(point_data[69] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[70]);
-- 
